2026-06-30 15:49:58 | INFO | summarizer.py:93 | execute | Summarizer memory[7]: [{'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': 'Now let me add reflections about the newly gained knowledge from this session.'}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'call_00_E7t8fGwaP4UD7uagK0rJ5330', 'name': 'edit_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/macbook/.copaw/workspaces/default/memory/2026-06-30.md', 'new_text': '### Media Upload API\n- `POST /api/media/file` accepts JSON payload: `{path, data (base64), fileName, mimeType, contextPath?}`\n- Returns `{file, assetsFile, imageUrl}` with the path to uploaded file\n- Max file size: 10 MB\n- Files are stored in `awn-storage/media/` under the manifest path\n- Uploaded media can be accessed via `/api/media/file?path=...&file=...`\n\n### Topic/Node Creation When Deleted\n- If a topic (folder with manifest.md) is deleted externally, `create_external_memory` and `write_external_memory` fail because the topic is not registered in the system\n- Workaround: manually create the folder and manifest.md via `write_file`, then create agent files directly as `.md` files in the folder\n- However, files created via `write_file` in the folder are NOT picked up by `list_external_memory` — they remain as raw files, not registered as multi-file memory in the virtual awn-storage layer\n- To properly restore a deleted topic with multi-file memory, the system likely needs a restart or the topic needs to be registered via the official API\n\n### Finding Game Covers on Russian Wikipedia\n- Russian Wikipedia images can be listed via: `action=query&list=allimages&aiprefix=<name>&format=json`\n- Cover files often have naming pattern: `Дальнобойщики.jpg`, `Дальнобойщики_3_-_Покорение_Америки.jpg`\n- ❌ `Дальнобойщики.jpg` is actually for the TV series, not the game\n- Verified game covers from Wikipedia RU:\n   - First game: `Дальнобойщики - Путь к победе (скриншот).jpg` (screenshot used as cover)\n   - Second game: `Дальнобойщики 2 (8.1).jpg` (proper box art)\n   - Third game: `Дальнобойщики 3 - Покорение Америки.jpg` (proper box art)\n   - Transport company: `Daltrkomp.jpg` (proper box art)\n\n### Claw Agents Ecosystem Details\n- **OpenClaw** (openclaw.ai) — 381k⭐ — TypeScript — MIT — personal AI assistant\n- **Agent Zero** (agent-zero.ai) — minimal agent, repo: agent0ai/agent-zero\n- **Hermes Agent** (hermes-agent.nousresearch.com) — by Nous Research, gbrain (Garry Tan) 24.6k⭐\n- **CoPaw** (copaw.ai) — self-hosted multi-channel, pip install copaw-aya, Docker available\n- **ZeroClaw** (zeroclaw.org) — Rust-based, 5MB RAM, cargo install\n- **MicroClaw** (microclaw.ai) — Rust CLI, cargo/npm install, 726⭐\n- **MetaClaw** (metaclaw.bot) — self-learning/evolving agent, Python, 3.4k⭐\n- Single-file memory (main.md) contains detailed configuration/CLI commands for each agent\n- ClawsHub — skill + plugin registry (9.1k⭐)', 'old_text': '### External Memory Management'}, 'raw_input': '{"file_path": "/Users/macbook/.copaw/workspaces/default/memory/2026-06-30.md", "new_text": "### Media Upload API\\n- `POST /api/media/file` accepts JSON payload: `{path, data (base64), fileName, mimeType, contextPath?}`\\n- Returns `{file, assetsFile, imageUrl}` with the path to uploaded file\\n- Max file size: 10 MB\\n- Files are stored in `awn-storage/media/` under the manifest path\\n- Uploaded media can be accessed via `/api/media/file?path=...&file=...`\\n\\n### Topic/Node Creation When Deleted\\n- If a topic (folder with manifest.md) is deleted externally, `create_external_memory` and `write_external_memory` fail because the topic is not registered in the system\\n- Workaround: manually create the folder and manifest.md via `write_file`, then create agent files directly as `.md` files in the folder\\n- However, files created via `write_file` in the folder are NOT picked up by `list_external_memory` — they remain as raw files, not registered as multi-file memory in the virtual awn-storage layer\\n- To properly restore a deleted topic with multi-file memory, the system likely needs a restart or the topic needs to be registered via the official API\\n\\n### Finding Game Covers on Russian Wikipedia\\n- Russian Wikipedia images can be listed via: `action=query&list=allimages&aiprefix=<name>&format=json`\\n- Cover files often have naming pattern: `Дальнобойщики.jpg`, `Дальнобойщики_3_-_Покорение_Америки.jpg`\\n- ❌ `Дальнобойщики.jpg` is actually for the TV series, not the game\\n- Verified game covers from Wikipedia RU:\\n   - First game: `Дальнобойщики - Путь к победе (скриншот).jpg` (screenshot used as cover)\\n   - Second game: `Дальнобойщики 2 (8.1).jpg` (proper box art)\\n   - Third game: `Дальнобойщики 3 - Покорение Америки.jpg` (proper box art)\\n   - Transport company: `Daltrkomp.jpg` (proper box art)\\n\\n### Claw Agents Ecosystem Details\\n- **OpenClaw** (openclaw.ai) — 381k⭐ — TypeScript — MIT — personal AI assistant\\n- **Agent Zero** (agent-zero.ai) — minimal agent, repo: agent0ai/agent-zero\\n- **Hermes Agent** (hermes-agent.nousresearch.com) — by Nous Research, gbrain (Garry Tan) 24.6k⭐\\n- **CoPaw** (copaw.ai) — self-hosted multi-channel, pip install copaw-aya, Docker available\\n- **ZeroClaw** (zeroclaw.org) — Rust-based, 5MB RAM, cargo install\\n- **MicroClaw** (microclaw.ai) — Rust CLI, cargo/npm install, 726⭐\\n- **MetaClaw** (metaclaw.bot) — self-learning/evolving agent, Python, 3.4k⭐\\n- Single-file memory (main.md) contains detailed configuration/CLI commands for each agent\\n- ClawsHub — skill + plugin registry (9.1k⭐)", "old_text": "### External Memory Management"}'}]
